{"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/FeaturesAndInput","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"How the app’s reducers fit together, and how a touch or a key press reaches the Mac without passing through them.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app keeps two kinds of work apart. Every decision a person can see, such as which capture card is open, which path carries video and which carries input, or whether the settings sheet is up, is state in a reducer and is tested with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TestStore"},{"type":"text","text":". Work that happens per frame, per input event, or per audio sample never goes through the store: reducers start it, configure it, and switch it, and it runs on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The feature tree","level":2,"anchor":"The-feature-tree"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppFeature","isActive":true},{"text":" is the root and the one screen. It scopes these child features:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/StreamFeature","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the capture session pointed at the right device and reports what the stream is doing, including the card’s status and the rectangle the Mac’s picture is drawn in."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityFeature"},{"text":" keeps each video and input path’s health, asks ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/PathSelector"},{"text":" for the live pair, and decides when a backup stream runs. It publishes the result as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityStatus"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SoundFeature"},{"text":" plays the Mac’s sound from whichever video is shown.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MacDisplayFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" asks the helper to mirror the Mac or extend it onto this screen while the helper’s stream is shown.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/HelperPairingFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" asks before the helper link pairs over the Bluetooth bond."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/UntypedTextFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names the characters Bluetooth couldn’t type.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SettingsFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is presented as the settings sheet and scopes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectionSettingsFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/CardProfilesFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SoundSettingsFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The root forwards changes between siblings. When the stream’s card status changes, connectivity hears of it. When connectivity changes the shown video, the stream and the Mac display feature hear of it. When the picture’s rectangle changes, the input path is told the size the Mac’s picture is drawn at.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"From-a-touch-to-the-Mac","type":"heading","text":"From a touch to the Mac"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurface","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" puts an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurfaceUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" over the video. The view is first responder while input is active, so it receives touches, Pencil, pointer, and hardware key presses. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MouseInput","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" feeds GameController mouse motion and buttons, which report raw relative motion even while the pointer is locked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each surface’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRouter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns that input into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InputEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" values in arrival order. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TouchInputMapper","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" maps gestures for the pointer mode in effect, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/KeyboardTracker","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps each key down at most once, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ButtonMerger","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" merges a click that arrives from both GameController and UIKit into one press. Every router and the mouse share one serial queue, so the main thread’s load can’t delay mouse events and there is a single order across all of them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The router hands each event to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which delivers it through the one "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputDelivery","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Delivery shapes every event with the person’s pointer speed and scroll direction, then passes it to the active input sink: the Bluetooth HID sink, or the helper link’s sink on one transport."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" decides which path is active. To switch, it takes the new path’s sink from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSinksClient"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switchTo"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivery releases every key and button on the old sink and waits for that, for at most 150 ms, before the new sink hears anything. Events that arrive meanwhile are held and replayed in order on the new sink, except the ups for keys and buttons the release already covered."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The on-screen keyboard takes a different route into the same router. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TextEntryView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reports each edit as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TextEdit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", the backspaces and new text the Mac must see, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/HardwareKeyForwarding"},{"type":"text","text":" says which hardware keys go to the Mac while that view is first responder. The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/KeyRow"},{"text":"‘s keys, for the keys iPadOS won’t pass to an app, are submitted through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient"},{"text":" so they keep their place among the surfaces’ events.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppFeature","doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppView"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Headwire"}],"title":"Features and the input path"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwire\/featuresandinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/StreamFeature":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/StreamFeature","title":"StreamFeature","abstract":[{"text":"Keeps the capture session pointed at the right device and reports what the stream is doing.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StreamFeature"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/streamfeature","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StreamFeature"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/InputDelivery":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InputDelivery","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InputDelivery","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"InputDelivery","url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/inputdelivery","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputDelivery","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The one place every input router delivers to: the active input sink, and the switch between sinks.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/MouseInput":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MouseInput","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MouseInput","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Feeds GameController mouse motion and buttons into the router while enabled.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MouseInput","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/mouseinput","title":"MouseInput"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/InputSinksClient":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSinksClient","title":"InputSinksClient","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sink that realises each input path, for the input router to switch to."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputSinksClient"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/inputsinksclient","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputSinksClient"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/ButtonMerger":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ButtonMerger","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ButtonMerger"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Merges button presses that reach the app twice into one press per click.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ButtonMerger"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/buttonmerger","title":"ButtonMerger"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/CardProfilesFeature":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The capture cards Headwire has seen, under Settings, Advanced; each opens its profile."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CardProfilesFeature"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"CardProfilesFeature","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/CardProfilesFeature","url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/cardprofilesfeature","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CardProfilesFeature"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/KeyRow":{"type":"topic","title":"KeyRow","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/KeyRow","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyRow","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KeyRow","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/keyrow","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A glass row of the keys iPadOS won’t pass to the app: back and forward, Mission Control, Apps, brightness and media.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/MacDisplayFeature":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MacDisplayFeature","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MacDisplayFeature"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Asks the helper to mirror the Mac or extend it onto this screen, as the person chose, while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the helper’s stream is what’s shown."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MacDisplayFeature"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/macdisplayfeature","title":"MacDisplayFeature"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/PathSelector":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/PathSelector","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PathSelector"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Chooses the video and input paths from their health and the person’s choices.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PathSelector"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/pathselector","title":"PathSelector"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/HelperPairingFeature":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/HelperPairingFeature","title":"HelperPairingFeature","abstract":[{"text":"Pairs the helper link over the Bluetooth bond, once the person allows it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HelperPairingFeature"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/helperpairingfeature","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HelperPairingFeature"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/TextEntryView":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TextEntryView","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextEntryView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An invisible text view that takes the on-screen keyboard and dictation, and reports each edit.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextEntryView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/textentryview","title":"TextEntryView"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/InputRoutingClient":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Says which input path receives the input layer’s events, and switches between paths."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputRoutingClient"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"InputRoutingClient","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient","url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/inputroutingclient","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputRoutingClient"}]},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/SettingsFeature":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/settingsfeature","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SettingsFeature","abstract":[{"text":"The settings sheet: capture device and format, display scaling, the Mac to send input to, and input preferences.","type":"text"}],"title":"SettingsFeature","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SettingsFeature","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SettingsFeature","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/InputRouter":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRouter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputRouter"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The input hot path: takes keyboard, mouse, and touch input and emits input events in arrival order.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputRouter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwire\/inputrouter","title":"InputRouter"},"doc://com.nth.headwire/documentation/Headwire/SoundSettingsFeature":{"